# pilot_new_branches/ is the September staging area from BUILDING the civil and
# industrial branches - large reference PDFs, draft templates, a testset preview.
# It is not the evaluation pilot; it held only those two branches because those
# were the two being built. Superseded by data/templates/branches/ (all five) and
# docs/references/. Kept locally, not committed, except the README that says so.
pilot_new_branches/*
!pilot_new_branches/README.md

# evaluator_pilot_17092026/ is the evaluation pilot, and its code and frozen slice ARE
# committed. The freeze is the record that 300 annotated traces were labelled
# against a specific set of items: untracked, it cannot be verified later, which
# is the one thing a freeze is for. Only the model outputs are held back, matching
# how inference_results/ is treated above.
evaluator_pilot_17092026/traces/
# Evaluator outputs, like traces, are produced data. The venv holds torch and the
# scorer stack for E0, isolated so the pilot does not change the system Python.
evaluator_pilot_17092026/scores/
evaluator_pilot_17092026/.venv/

scratch/

# docs/references: large source binaries are NOT committed. MANIFEST.json records
# each one's URL and SHA-256, and fetch_references.py re-acquires and verifies
# them on any checkout. The small text/TSV/HTML/JSON sources ARE committed.
docs/references/**/*.pdf
docs/references/**/*.zip
docs/references/**/*.xlsx
